# One session's loop over a derived artifact: render it, edit an input, read it.
#
# The fixture drives the REAL `le hook-check` binary against a scratch checkout
# and judges the file the hooks leave behind. Three facts are owed, and each has
# its own marker: a session start renders an artifact the tree does not hold, a
# write to one of its inputs REMOVES it, and a command naming it rebuilds it
# before that command runs.
#
# The last marker is the one a tracked artifact could never earn. A committed
# copy answered the read from whatever the previous commit held, with nothing in
# the tree to say the inputs had moved since.
#
# The scenario rides ai/CODE-TO-DOCS.md rather than ai/PACKAGE-MAP.md because the
# posttool-writeedit chain also lints an edited Go file, which would put
# golangci-lint's verdict in this loop's exit code. The package map's own loop is
# proved by TestAGrepAfterAnEditReadsTheEditedPackage
# (internal/le/derived/derived_test.go), through the same two checks.

option=timeout:value=120s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test fixture runner/le-derived-artifact-lifecycle
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=derived-fixture-ready
expect=stdout:contains=session-start-rendered-the-artifact
expect=stdout:contains=input-write-removed-the-artifact
expect=stdout:contains=read-materialized-the-artifact
expect=stdout:contains=grep-read-the-edited-tree
